cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "FIMsens: a modular multi-sensor toolset for flood extent and depth mapping"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Tian
    given-names: Dan
    email: tiandan.geo@gmail.com
    affiliation: University of Alabama
repository-code: "https://github.com/tian-dandan/fimsens"
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-08-18"
keywords:
  - flood mapping
  - flood inundation
  - synthetic aperture radar
  - Sentinel-1
  - remote sensing
  - water surface elevation
  - flood depth
abstract: >-
  FIMsens is a Python toolset that turns incomplete and partly unreliable
  satellite observations into hydrologically consistent flood extent and depth
  information. Rather than treating flood mapping as a single water-classification
  step, it applies a progressive flood-evidence refinement framework: discover
  suitable observations, detect directly observable floodwater with Seeded Local
  Adaptive Thresholding (SLAT), assess which detected flood objects are physically
  plausible with the Flood Object Reliability Filter (FOR-Filter), then reconstruct
  omitted inundation and estimate depth from topography with RS-FloodXDepth.
  Directly observed and reconstructed inundation are kept as separate classes, and
  intermediate outputs are preserved, so users can trace how a final map was
  produced.

